{{1983 Pacific-10 Conference football standings}}
The '''1983 Oregon State Beavers football team''' represented [[Oregon State University]] as a remember of [[Pac-12 Conference|Pacific-10 Conference]] (Pac-10) during the [[1983 NCAA Division I-A football season]]. In their fourth season under head coach [[Joe Avezzano]], compiled an overall record of 3–7–1 record with a mark of  1–6–1 in conference playing, placing ninth in the Pac-10. 1983 was Oregon State's 13th consecutive losing season. The Beavers scored 171 points and allowed 332 points. The season is most memorable for the 0–0 tie with [[1983 Oregon Ducks football team|Oregon]] in the [[Oregon–Oregon State football rivalry|Civil War]], the last scoreless game in [[NCAA Division I]] football history. The game is known colloquially as the "[[1983 Oregon State vs. Oregon football game|Toilet Bowl]]."

